// Tarjan's strongly connected components over the digest's call graph.
//
// A case's key has to change when anything its function can reach changes,
// and recursion means "what it can reach" is not a tree. Collapsing each cycle
// into one component makes it a DAG, and Tarjan completes the components in
// an order where every component a component reaches is already complete --
// so each one's hash is computed once, from its members and its callees'
// finished hashes (../seal/), in one pass over the graph: linear, where a
// reachability walk per case would be quadratic in a compiler-sized program.

dg_scc_all() {
  int dgv = 0;
  while(dgv < len((import dg_ix))) {
    dg_try(dgv);
    dgv = dgv + 1;
  }
} return void;
